abstract="In spatially complex and hand-busy contexts, traditional menu-based web browsing imposes interaction constraints. This paper extends a framework originally conceived for goal-driven web interfaces to eXtended Reality (XR) and discusses how LLMs can be leveraged to dynamically orchestrate pervasive interfaces for the Web, decomposing natural language intents into executable user interface components. A user study shows that AI-driven orchestration of XR Web interfaces supports effective interaction with low perceived workload, while highlighting open challenges in intent interpretation and context management.",
